# Locked hardware (draft)

Full text: [docs/context/01-master-constitution.md](docs/context/01-master-constitution.md), [docs/context/02-hardware-firmware.md](docs/context/02-hardware-firmware.md).

Candidate locks (not applied to existing BSP until conflict sign-off):

- PMS5003 (UART PM), SCD41 (I²C CO₂/T/RH @ 0x62), BME688 (I²C T/RH/P/gas features @ 0x76/0x77), MQ135 (conditioned ADC, not ppm), ESP32-DevKitC-32E, SX1278 @ 433 MHz, Raspberry Pi 5.
- GPS/GNSS is not used. No GPS UART, PPS, parser, or coordinates in node packets. Location lives in gateway node registry.
- Wi-Fi/BLE are not the field telemetry path.
- Keep GPIO in one config layer. Candidate map: I²C 21/22, PMS UART RX16/TX17, LoRa SPI 18/23/19 CS5, RST14, DIO0 25, MQ135 ADC 34, LED 2.
- Do not scatter pin numbers. MQ135 divider ratio is configuration, not a magic number.
- Do not retune LoRa to 868/915 MHz without an explicit hardware reopen.
- Do not hard-code exactly five nodes. Configurable `node_id`.

Existing firmware BSP and ADRs currently disagree on several of these. See [docs/context/CONFLICT_MATRIX.md](docs/context/CONFLICT_MATRIX.md).
